question.explanation:
for each element (2 x 2 marks)
2 marks – Describes how the element is used on the menu board and its purpose
1 mark – Names the element with little description

for each choice (2 x 2 marks)
2 marks – Names a typography part and describes a choice with a reason linked to the residents (e.g. body text at least 14 pt so it can be read without glasses)
1 mark – States a choice with no reason

for each modification (2 x 2 marks)
2 marks – Describes a change and how it meets the need (e.g. make the Saturday hours larger and bold so they are the focal point)
1 mark – States a change

for each purpose (2 x 2 marks)
2 marks – Describes a purpose and how it helps the user
1 mark – Names a purpose only

for each consideration (2 x 2 marks)
2 marks – Explains cost, specifications or user needs linked to the practice
1 mark – States a consideration with no link

for each strategy (2 x 2 marks)
2 marks – Describes a strategy and why it helps (e.g. install air-conditioning set to about 20 to 24 degrees Celsius; add ventilation; keep vents clear)
1 mark – States a strategy

for each change (2 x 2 marks)
2 marks – Describes a change and how it protects her (e.g. set the account to private so only approved followers see her videos)
1 mark – States a change with no reason

for each benefit (2 x 2 marks)
2 marks – Explains a benefit linked to the agency (e.g. staff can search by address and find the right contract quickly)
1 mark – States a benefit

for each feature (2 x 2 marks)
2 marks – Describes a feature and how it helps this ad (e.g. trim to remove unneeded parts so the ad is 30 seconds)
1 mark – Names a feature only

for each check (2 x 2 marks)
2 marks – Describes a check and why (e.g. download from the official developer site so it is not bundled with malware; check minimum requirements)
1 mark – States a check

for each change (2 x 2 marks)
2 marks – Describes a change and how it helps (e.g. remove blank rows and add a Category column so the data can be sorted and filtered)
1 mark – States a change

for each characteristic (2 x 2 marks)
2 marks – Describes a characteristic and links it to a design decision (e.g. adults over 50 may be new to boxing, so show beginners, not fit athletes)
1 mark – States a characteristic with no link to the design

for each annotation (2 x 2 marks)
2 marks – Describes a specific annotation with the reason for the choice (e.g. menu across the top so customers find Bookings on every page)
1 mark – Gives a label with no reason

for each method (2 x 2 marks)
2 marks – Describes a method and what evidence it gives (e.g. survey 10 students to rate whether the video made them want to attend)
1 mark – Names a method only

for each use (2 x 2 marks)
2 marks – Label: lossless (e.g. WAV/FLAC) because mastering needs every detail. Fans: lossy (MP3) because small files download quickly and quality loss is barely heard
1 mark – Correct type with a general reason

for each strategy (2 x 2 marks)
2 marks – Describes a strategy and its benefit for the group
1 mark – States a strategy

for each strategy (2 x 2 marks)
2 marks – Describes a strategy and how it solves her problem (e.g. one master in OneDrive with version history; names with version numbers and dates)
1 mark – States a strategy

for each tool (2 x 2 marks)
2 marks – Describes a tool and its effect on this laptop (e.g. disk clean-up removes temporary files, freeing space on the full SSD)
1 mark – Names a tool

for each way (2 x 2 marks)
2 marks – Describes a tool or habit and how it protects (e.g. run an updated anti-malware scan to find and remove the spyware)
1 mark – States a way

for each device (2 x 2 marks)
2 marks – Router: directs data between the studio's LAN and the internet. Modem: converts the provider's signal so the network can connect to the internet
1 mark – States a general purpose

for each device (2 x 2 marks)
2 marks – Placement and reason linked to the home (e.g. router at the NBN point in the garage; wireless access point upstairs so bedrooms get a strong signal through the floor)
1 mark – Placement with no reason

for each responsibility (2 x 2 marks)
2 marks – Explains a responsibility (e.g. keep data secure; notify customers and the regulator of a serious breach; destroy data no longer needed)
1 mark – States a responsibility

for each group (2 x 2 marks)
2 marks – Explains an effect on a named group (e.g. older residents without app skills must travel to another town to bank)
1 mark – States an effect

for each type (2 x 2 marks)
2 marks – Describes a type and how it helps this group
1 mark – Names a type only

